# === Frontend Configuration ===

# Backend API Gateway URL (required)
# Get from: sam deploy output or AWS CloudFormation console
EXPO_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=https://your-api-gateway-url.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com

# Feature flags for ML migration
# Canonical source: frontend/src/config/features.ts
EXPO_PUBLIC_BROWSER_SENTIMENT=true           # Default: true (browser-based sentiment analysis)
EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_LAMBDA_SENTIMENT=true        # Default: true (Lambda sentiment with local fallback)
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BROWSER_PREDICTION is gone. Predictions are server-side only; the
# flag was read nowhere and features.test.ts asserts FeatureFlags does not carry it.

# Logging verbosity (optional — default: debug in dev, warn in production)
# EXPO_PUBLIC_LOG_LEVEL=warn                  # Options: error, warn, info, debug

# [Pro] Cognito authentication (optional — app works without auth)
# EXPO_PUBLIC_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=us-east-1_xxxxx
# EXPO_PUBLIC_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=xxxxx

# === Backend Configuration ===

FINNHUB_API_KEY=your_finnhub_api_key         # Required — get from https://finnhub.io
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=*                            # CORS origins (default: *) — see the note below

# ALLOWED_ORIGINS, in production
# ------------------------------
# A comma-separated allow-list must name EVERY origin that calls the API,
# including the admin dashboard's own CloudFront domain. The admin API honours
# this list as of this release; before that it answered
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * unconditionally, because AdminFunction carried
# no ALLOWED_ORIGINS at all. A deployment locked down to the public web origin
# alone will have the admin SPA's requests blocked by the browser, because the
# SPA is served from the AdminCloudFrontUrl stack output
# (https://<distribution>.cloudfront.net) and that origin will not be on the
# list. The symptom looks like a broken deploy and is a config omission.
#
# A malformed list fails CLOSED: response.util.ts omits the CORS header rather
# than falling back to '*', so a typo here disables CORS entirely rather than
# loosening it.
#
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-domain.example,https://dxxxxxxxxxxxxx.cloudfront.net

# Optional backend env vars (set in template.yaml or .env.deploy)
# ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY=                     # Alpha Vantage API (optional data source)
# ML_SENTIMENT_API_URL=                      # Primary ML sentiment API endpoint
# DISTILFINBERT_API_URL=                     # ML sentiment fallback (used when ML_SENTIMENT_API_URL is not set)
# LOG_LEVEL=info                             # Logging verbosity: error, warn, info, debug
# COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=                      # [Pro] Backend Cognito integration (JWT issuer)
# COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=                         # [Pro] Backend Cognito app client ID (JWT audience)
# SES_FROM_EMAIL=                            # [Pro] SES verified sender for reports and alerts

# === [Pro] Operational settings whose absence fails silently ===
# Both are read by backend/scripts/deploy.sh and passed to template.yaml.
# Neither has a safe default, and neither failure mode raises an error.
#
# ALARM_EMAIL — SNS destination for every CloudWatch alarm in the stack. There
# are 35 of them. AlarmEmailSubscription carries Condition: HasAlarmEmail and
# the parameter defaults to empty, so until this is set the alarms change state
# in the console and tell nobody. AWS sends a confirmation email that must be
# accepted before any notification is delivered.
# ALARM_EMAIL=ops@your-domain.example
#
# FINNHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET — shared secret for POST /webhooks/finnhub, compared
# constant-time against the X-Finnhub-Secret header. When unset the handler
# answers 503 to every event: fail-closed by design, because an open ingestion
# endpoint lets anyone inject tickers. Finnhub disables an endpoint that fails
# to acknowledge events over consecutive days, so the observable symptom is
# ingestion simply stopping.
# FINNHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your_long_random_string

# === [Pro] Stripe Billing ===
# Required for the billing handler and webhook receiver. When any of these
# are unset, billing is disabled: /stripe/checkout and /stripe/portal reply
# "Billing not configured" (HTTP 500), and /stripe/webhook replies "Webhook
# not configured" (HTTP 500). The rest of the app continues to work and
# free-tier users are unaffected; community/free deployments can leave the
# block commented out.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxxxx            # Secret key from Stripe dashboard (Developers > API keys)
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_xxxxx          # Webhook signing secret (Developers > Webhooks > endpoint)
# STRIPE_PRICE_ID_MONTHLY=price_xxxxx        # Price ID for the monthly Pro plan
# PUBLIC_WEB_URL=https://your-domain.example  # PLACEHOLDER — must be a real origin your deployment serves.
#                                            # Base URL for checkout success / cancel and billing-portal
#                                            # returns; Stripe redirects users here after payment.

# === [Pro] Social Sentiment ===
# Reddit OAuth app credentials used by the social-sentiment service to fetch
# subreddit chatter. When unset, the Reddit feed is disabled and the
# social-sentiment endpoint falls back to Finnhub signals only (no error
# surfaced to the user).
# REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=                          # Reddit OAuth app client ID (script-type app)
# REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=                      # Reddit OAuth app client secret

# === Backend Infrastructure ===
# Set automatically by the SAM template; override only for local testing.
# SENTIMENT_QUEUE_URL=                       # SQS queue URL for the SentimentWorker

# === Admin Configuration (optional) ===
# These are set automatically by SAM template — only override for local testing
# STACK_NAME=                                # CloudFormation stack name for CloudWatch queries
# API_ID=                                    # API Gateway ID for metrics
# LAMBDA_MEMORY_MB=512                       # Lambda memory for cost calculations

# === SAM Template Parameters ===
# AlertSweepInterval: EventBridge rate expression for alert sweep frequency
#   Default: 'rate(4 hours)' — valid values: any EventBridge rate or cron expression
#   Set in template.yaml parameters or via sam deploy --parameter-overrides

# === Local Development (optional — used with `make ministack`) ===
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1                       # Set by Lambda at runtime; override locally only
# DYNAMODB_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4566
# DYNAMODB_TABLE_NAME=react-stocks-local-Table
